From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 01:29:25 +0200
Subject: ARM: dts: allwinner: sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711: Smooth backlight brightness
 scale

Drop the 10-entry doubling brightness-levels table. Without a table
pwm-backlight generates its default CIE 1931 perceptual table with
period/fls(period) = 3125 levels for the 50us period, the same fine
scale the PinePhone uses. The old table gave 9 visible steps with
the brightness doubling at each one.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts
@@ -75,8 +75,12 @@ backlight: backlight {
 		pwms = <&pwm 0 50000 PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED>;
 		enable-gpios = <&pio 3 29 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		power-supply = <&reg_sw>;
-		brightness-levels = <0 1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 255>;
-		default-brightness-level = <9>;
+		/*
+		 * No brightness-levels table: pwm-backlight then builds its
+		 * default CIE 1931 table with period/fls(period) = 3125
+		 * levels, the same fine perceptual scale the PinePhone gets.
+		 * The old 10-entry doubling table gave 9 visible steps.
+		 */
 	};
 
 	i2c_gpio: i2c-gpio {
-- 
Armbian

